    "datePosted": "2026-11-13T07:20:30.000Z",
    "description": "Position Overview / Scope of Role The Sales Representative – Van-Based Sales is responsible for directly selling and distributing company products to customers within assigned sales territories using a company-provided vehicle. The position focuses on developing customer relationships, expanding market coverage, achieving assigned sales targets, and ensuring effective distribution of company products through direct and route-based selling activities. The role requires independently managing daily sales operations, including customer visits, product promotion, order taking, cash collection, receipt issuance, and reconciliation of daily sales transactions. The Sales Representative is also accountable for the proper handling of company products, sales proceeds, receipts, and assigned vehicle while ensuring customer satisfaction and compliance with established sales and operational procedures. Top Roles and Responsibilities Direct Sales and Product Distribution Conduct direct sales and distribution of company products using an assigned company vehicle within designated sales territories. Visit existing and potential customers, retailers, wholesalers, shops, supermarkets, and other relevant outlets to promote and sell company products. Ensure the timely delivery and availability of products to customers in assigned routes and territories. Introduce company products to potential customers and communicate product features, benefits, pricing, and promotional offers. Identify new sales opportunities and expand the company's customer base and market coverage. Maintain regular contact with existing customers to strengthen business relationships and encourage repeat purchases. Ensure proper product handling, loading, unloading, and delivery to maintain product quality and prevent damage. Sales Target Achievement and Market Development Achieve daily, weekly, and monthly sales targets assigned by the immediate supervisor. Implement approved sales plans and route coverage schedules to maximize sales opportunities. Identify potential customers, new outlets, and underserved market areas within assigned territories. Monitor customer demand, purchasing patterns, competitor activities, and market developments and report relevant findings. Recommend opportunities for improving product distribution, market penetration, and sales performance. Follow up with customers to maintain regular purchases and improve customer retention. Customer Relationship and Service Management Maintain professional relationships with customers and provide timely and appropriate sales support. Respond to customer inquiries regarding product availability, prices, quality, and delivery arrangements. Handle customer complaints and product-related concerns professionally and report issues requiring management attention. Ensure accurate communication of approved prices, discounts, promotional offers, and sales terms. Maintain a positive company image through professional conduct and responsible customer service. Cash Collection, Receipt Issuance, and Sales Transaction Management Collect payments from customers for products sold in accordance with approved company payment procedures. Issue official company receipts for every sales transaction using assigned receipt books or approved electronic systems. Independently operate the assigned cash register, POS device, or other approved sales transaction system. Ensure that all sales, cash collections, credit transactions (where authorized), and returns are properly recorded and documented. Maintain accurate records of daily sales transactions, customer payments, receipts issued, and outstanding balances. Safeguard all cash collected, receipt books, cash register records, and other financial documents under personal responsibility. Ensure that collected cash and sales proceeds are properly submitted to the designated cashier or finance office within the required timeframe. Stock Management and Daily Reconciliation Verify the quantity and condition of products received before commencing daily sales activities. Maintain accurate records of products loaded, sold, returned, damaged, and remaining in the assigned vehicle. Reconcile daily sales quantities against issued stock, remaining inventory, returned products, and supporting documents. Ensure that all stock movements are properly documented and reported. Immediately report stock shortages, discrepancies, damaged products, or unexplained losses. Ensure proper accountability for all company products assigned for daily sales and distribution. Sales Reporting and Documentation Prepare and submit daily sales reports detailing sales volume, revenue, customer visits, cash collections, and unsold stock. Maintain accurate customer records, sales transaction documents, receipt records, and route coverage reports. Report market conditions, customer feedback, competitor activities, and emerging sales opportunities to the immediate supervisor. Provide timely updates on sales performance, challenges, and operational issues affecting assigned territories. Ensure that all sales and distribution documents are complete, accurate, and submitted within established deadlines. Company Vehicle Management and Compliance Operate the assigned company vehicle responsibly and in accordance with traffic regulations and company vehicle management procedures. Conduct routine vehicle inspections and ensure that the assigned vehicle is maintained in good operating condition. Ensure proper loading, transportation, and unloading of company products. Maintain vehicle cleanliness and report mechanical problems, accidents, damages, or maintenance requirements promptly. Use the company vehicle exclusively for authorized business activities. Maintain accountability for the vehicle, products, equipment, and other company property assigned. Performs other related duties as directed.",
