    "description": "Position Overview / Scope of Role The Quality Assurance Officer is responsible for monitoring, inspecting, and controlling the quality of coffee and related products throughout the processing and production stages to ensure compliance with established quality standards, product specifications, food safety requirements, and applicable regulatory standards. The position oversees quality inspection of incoming raw coffee, monitors quality parameters throughout coffee processing operations, conducts or coordinates laboratory testing and sensory evaluation, and ensures that finished products meet the required quality specifications before storage, packaging, and dispatch. The role also identifies quality deviations, recommends corrective actions, and supports continuous improvement of coffee processing operations to maintain product consistency, quality, and customer satisfaction. Top Roles and Responsibilities Raw Material Quality Inspection and Control Inspect and assess incoming raw coffee beans and other production materials to ensure compliance with established quality specifications. Monitor the physical condition, moisture content, cleanliness, and general quality of raw coffee beans. Identify defects, foreign materials, contamination, and other quality deviations in incoming coffee materials. Ensure proper sampling, inspection, testing, and documentation of incoming raw materials. Coordinate with procurement, warehouse, and production teams regarding raw material quality issues and acceptance or rejection recommendations. Ensure appropriate handling and storage conditions to preserve the quality of raw coffee beans. Coffee Processing Quality Control Monitor quality parameters throughout coffee processing operations, including cleaning, sorting, grading, roasting, grinding, and packaging, as applicable. Ensure that coffee processing activities comply with approved procedures, technical specifications, and established quality standards. Monitor critical processing parameters, including moisture content, roasting consistency, particle size, and other relevant product characteristics. Conduct regular inspections at different stages of production to identify process deviations and prevent quality deterioration. Ensure consistency in processing outputs and adherence to approved product specifications. Work closely with production personnel to address quality-related challenges and improve processing practices. Laboratory Testing and Quality Assessment Conduct and coordinate routine laboratory tests to assess the physical and chemical quality characteristics of raw materials, work-in-progress, and finished products. Perform appropriate quality tests, including moisture content, physical defect assessment, and other relevant chemical and physical analyses. Ensure proper sampling techniques, testing procedures, and handling of laboratory equipment. Maintain accurate laboratory records, test results, and quality assessment reports. Ensure that laboratory equipment and testing instruments are properly maintained, calibrated, and used in accordance with established procedures. Report test results and recommend appropriate actions where products fail to meet established quality requirements. Coffee Cupping and Sensory Evaluation Conduct or coordinate coffee cupping and sensory evaluation to assess coffee aroma, flavor, acidity, body, balance, aftertaste, and overall cup quality. Evaluate coffee samples against established quality standards and product profiles. Identify sensory defects and inconsistencies that may affect product quality and customer acceptance. Maintain sensory evaluation records and communicate findings to production and management. Support the development and maintenance of consistent coffee quality profiles for different products and customer requirements. Food Safety, Hygiene, and Regulatory Compliance Monitor compliance with applicable food safety standards, hygiene requirements, sanitation procedures, and quality management systems. Ensure that production and processing areas meet required cleanliness and food safety standards. Monitor potential contamination risks during raw material handling, processing, storage, and packaging. Ensure compliance with applicable national quality standards, regulatory requirements, and relevant industry standards. Participate in food safety inspections, internal audits, external audits, and quality certification activities. Identify non-compliance issues and follow up on corrective and preventive actions. Non-Conformance Management and Corrective Actions Identify, document, and report non-conforming raw materials, work-in-progress, and finished products. Investigate quality deviations, customer complaints, and processing-related quality problems in coordination with relevant departments. Recommend corrective and preventive actions to address identified quality issues. Monitor the implementation and effectiveness of corrective actions. Ensure that rejected, reprocessed, or non-conforming products are properly identified, documented, and controlled. Support root-cause analysis to prevent recurring quality problems. Quality Documentation and Reporting Maintain accurate quality inspection records, laboratory results, sensory evaluation reports, and product quality documentation. Prepare and submit regular quality assurance reports highlighting inspection results, quality trends, non-conformities, and corrective actions. Maintain appropriate records for raw material quality, production process inspections, finished product approval, and product traceability. Ensure that quality documentation is properly organized and available for internal and external audits. Report significant quality concerns and risks to the immediate supervisor and relevant management. Quality Improvement and Staff Awareness Recommend improvements to coffee processing methods, quality control procedures, and product handling practices. Work closely with production teams to improve product consistency and minimize quality losses. Provide technical guidance and awareness to production employees on quality standards, food safety, hygiene, and proper product handling. Participate in quality improvement initiatives, process reviews, and implementation of approved quality management systems. Monitor quality performance and recommend measures to improve product reliability and customer satisfaction. Performs other related duties as directed.",
