    "description": "Accountant Job by BAN-Development Research Centre for Excellence (BAN-DRCE) Are you an experienced and results-driven finance professional looking to take ownership of an organization's overall financial management? Do you have a strong commitment to accuracy, transparency and accountability, with a keen interest in financial reporting, budgeting, compliance and problem-solving? If this sounds like you, we welcome you to consider an exciting opportunity with the BAN-Development Research Center for Excellence (BAN-DRCE). We are in search of a talented, enthusiastic, and motivated Accountant to join our team. BAN-DRCE, a leading research and development organization, is on the lookout for a self-driven accountant who will lead and oversee our overall finance activities and collaborate closely with various teams to contribute to the successful execution of projects. Employment Type: Accountant Experience Required: Minimum of three years Duration: 2 Months of prohibition Period Duty Station: Addis Ababa Total Number: one Key Responsibilities: Oversee and manage the overall financial activities of the organization, including the general ledger, accounts payable and receivable, payroll, and cash management. Prepare accurate and timely monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements and management reports. Prepare, monitor, and control organizational and project budgets and forecasts track financial metrics and analyze variances from budgets. Maintain complete and accurate books of account in the accounting software (Peachtree), ensuring correct postings and regular bank and ledger reconciliations. Review and verify invoices, payment requests, and expense reports, ensuring accuracy, proper supporting documentation, and timely payment. Manage accounts payable and receivable, including follow-up clients. Review all project field expenses, including reconciliation of field budgets with actual expenses, and prepare a project expense report for each batch of field expenses. Prepare payment requests and invoices for clients in line with contract terms, and follow up the payment process until payment is received, tracking outstanding amounts and reporting on them. Prepare payments for the field team, including per diems, allowances, advances, and supplier payments, ensuring proper approvals and supporting documents. Manage the overall field financial process, including field cash advances, liquidation and settlement, field budget control, and guidance to field staff on financial procedures and documentation. Prepare cash flow plans and manage bank accounts and petty cash to ensure adequate liquidity for operations and projects. Process monthly payroll, including statutory deductions such as income tax and pension. Ensure compliance with taxation and other regulatory requirements (VAT, withholding tax, income tax, etc.) and prepare and submit timely filings. Provide financial reporting and related support to clients as needed, based on their specific requirements and agreed deadlines. Prepare and declare month, quarter taxes to the organization responsible Coordinate internal and external audits by preparing the necessary schedules, documentation, and information, and follow up on the implementation of audit recommendations. Develop, implement, and continuously improve financial policies, procedures, and internal controls, and ensure compliance with company policies and relevant regulations. Maintain the fixed asset register and manage depreciation and asset verification. Provide financial information, analysis, and advice to management to support decision-making. Serve as a point of contact for finance-related inquiries from other departments, and liaise with clients, banks, auditors, and tax authorities as needed. Guide and support administrative staff in day-to-day finance tasks. Organize and maintain financial files, both physical and electronic, with efficient filing systems, ensuring confidentiality and easy access. Basic Salary: As Per Company Scale",
